Xmalloc

A set of functions and libraries to wrap around malloc, that will provide
a log of the memory allocated. Which file, function and line-number that
allocated and how big each allocation was.

When malloc fails (perhaps due to memory exhaustion), xmalloc will
dump the entire log to stderr before returning NULL to the caller. 

This is needed because valgrind won't work with the GC in ECL, and therefore 
I cannot now determine if I am leaking memory when calling functions from
ECL. The only question is "is it possible to track memory access violations?"

This might be possible if we register a signal handler for access violations,
but it will be impossible to know if an access violation does not result in a
signal being raised (going one past the end of an array doesn't generate a
signal if the access only results in corruption of some other memory block
that the program can access).

